window.products.push({"id":116263,"name":"279570 Dryer Door Latch Kit Whirlpool Kenmore Maytag Strike Catch Part AP3094183 PS334230 3-Pack WED5000DW2 WED5700XW0 WGD9400SW0 WED9151YW0 WED49STBW","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":9.95,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51AA5bwRXmL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"💡 Whirlpool Door Latch Kit 279570 - An equivalent for parts AP3094183, 14205029, 14205577, 14210022, 2003, 236876, 236877, 241282, 241890, 26000279570, 261847, 263067, 279280, 279337, 279469, 279570VP, 291949, 3390239, 3392538, 3398175, 342295, 347813, 3493, 4165234, 51651001, 51655001, 66021, 690081, 690082, 693717, 694343, 696144, 8208, 830751, 834767, 834813, 834943, 834944, AH334230, DE902, EA334230, FSP279570, PS334230. Dryer Door Latch Kit 279570 comes with strike and catch. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace the Latch 279570 Kit? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. Dryer Door Catch 279570 will help if your appliance door doesn't close, doesn't start, shuts off too soon, or doesn't shut off. It is necessary to replace the catch immediately if it's not working properly. Running the dryer with a faulty catch may be unsafe as the door may remain open. 💡 Dryer Door Latch 279570 is compatible with Whirlpool, Admiral, Crosley, Estate, Inglis, KitchenAid, Magic Chef, Maytag, Roper, Kenmore appliance's. To keep your dryer door closed during the drying cycle, the strike is mounted on the dryer body and the catch is mounted on the door. The catch holds the strike and keeps the door closed. Whirlpool Dryer Door Catch 279570 Kit meets or exceeds all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 What tools do I need to install the 279570 Door Latch Kit? To install the kit, you will need basic tools such as a screwdriver, pliers, socket wrench, and the new hardware that comes with the kit. A flathead or Phillips screwdriver will be needed to remove the screws holding the old door catch and strike. Pliers can be useful to disconnect any wires or clips attached to the old door catch and strike. A socket wrench may be needed if the old door catch and strike are held in place with bolts. 💡 How long does it take to install the Part Number 279570? The time it takes to install the Kenmore Dryer Door Catch 279570 Kit will depend on your level of experience and familiarity with your dryer. On average, installation can take anywhere from 15 to 45 minutes. If you are experienced with DIY projects and have installed similar kits before, it may take less time. However, if you are a novice, it may take longer to complete the installation.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51AA5bwRXmL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B07MX5CQPL","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-116263","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07MX5CQPL","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B07MX5CQPL","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
